Z||000000||FieroBUZZ||10-22-2001||09:20 PM||||Or...why I own a Fiero..or two.  I decided tonight was the time to do one of those simple mods to my GT.  By gar, I'll add a fan switch.  Out came my trusty directions (in this case, thanks to  Standard) and tool box.  I probably dismantled much more than needed, but you know how it is once you get going.  Wired up my new little chrome toggle switch (I love little chrome toggle switches) and time to test.  Hey, that must be the 'off' direction.  What a coincidence, the other direction must be 'off' too! Sh*t!!  At least it looks cool.<P>As my car has never overheated and I've never actually seen the fan work, I guess this is one to track down.  As usual in working on my car, I discovered something.  Being built somewhat like one of MonkeyMan's less supple bretheren, I found a muscle in my shoulder that hates being twisted upside down under a Fiero dash.  How was YOUR day?<BR>Gary<BR>86 SE<BR>86 GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||Alex2004||10-22-2001||10:00 PM||||You might buy want to buy a new relay, i never noticed mine on before but it did get hot sometimes so i bought a new relay and i hear it kick on from time to time.  But before i bought that i was going to wire up a toggle switch.  I cannot remember how much it was, but i got it from GM. Just thought i'd let you know!<P>Alex...||||reg||3
Z||000002||Cheever3000||10-22-2001||10:47 PM||||I still want one of those boxes with a switch, and when you flip it a hand comes up & flips it again then the hand goes back in the box where it was.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||x-thumpr-x||10-22-2001||10:53 PM||||best first test to see if it is your relay. Find the single green wire on the engine (coolant line) un plug it and ground it somewhere. If your fan kicks in, your relay works, if not, your relay is fried! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sage||10-23-2001||06:47 AM||||If you take the connector to the relay(under the hood in front of the drivers side h/l), off the relay and jumper the two outside pins, the fan should come on with your ign. switch in the on position.  It will run constantly while the engine is running or the key is on, but it will tell you if the fan works also.<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
